# Only what the published map needs goes to GitHub: the atlas/ folder (the viewer, its data, symbols, fonts, glyphs and vendor
# libraries) plus the Pages workflow in .github/. GitHub Pages serves atlas/ and nothing else, so the rest stays on this computer.

# the map-building toolchain, its hand-made source data and the author's original material (kept locally, not published)
/tools/
/original_data/
/_backup_*/

# editor / assistant settings and scratch
/.claude/
node_modules/
*.log

# build leftovers inside atlas/ that the viewer never loads (alternative climate runs written by tools/climate.mjs)
/atlas/data/climate_natural.json
/atlas/data/climate_northeast.json
/atlas/data/climate_wall.json
/atlas/data/climate_west.json
